  final String remedies;

  /// UTF-8 JSON, canonical: an array with one entry per chart, each with a member for every reading the record asked and none for one it did not. `purified` is what the purifier of BPHS ch. 2 vv. 67-78 leaves standing of the window around the chart's instant, `{intervals, removed, edges, grid}`: each interval `{from, to, verdict}` with the clauses that held, each removed run naming the clause that failed. `conception` is `{birth, pranapadaHouse, nisheka, moon}` at the chart's instant (BPHS ch. 3 vv. 25-29, *Brihat Jataka* IV.21). `circumstance` is `{sky, father, presentation, lamp, attending, weights}` (*Brihat Jataka* ch. V), each fact given one weight. `baseline` is the baseline engine's unsourced cascade around the chart's instant, `{window, sunrise, intervals, intervalWidthMinutes, resolutionMinutes, suggested, concentration, candidates, stages, eventsUsed, eventsHeldOut, holdOut}`. `svarodaya` is the Shiva Svarodaya's nadi and tattva, `{at, runs}`: `at` the reading at the chart's instant `{sunrise, nextSunrise, tithi, sunriseNadi, run, junctions}` and `runs` every run `{from, to, nadi, turn, tattva, sex}` of the window around it, a report the text does not make at a birth. Instants are Julian days UTC. Empty when `rectification_json` asked for none.
  final String rectification;

  /// UTF-8 JSON, canonical: an array with one entry per chart, each `{reading, cycle, periods, year}` (`03-design/lalkitab.md`). `reading` is the teva's: `planets`, each `{graha, house, dignities, owners, awake, kayam, casts}` with `dignities` among `PAKKA`, `EXALTED`, `DEBILITATED` and `OWN`, `owners` each `{owner, regard}` (`FRIEND`, `EQUAL` or `ENEMY`) and `casts` each aspect `{to, strength, onto}` (`QUARTER`, `HALF` or `FULL`); `houses`, each `{house, occupants, lookedAtBy, awake, waker}` with `lookedAtBy` each `{from, strength}`; `masnui`, each pair in one house `{pair, house, countsAs}`; `rinas`, each debt `{rin, of, seated}` with `seated` each `{enemy, house}`; `pitri`, the ancestors' debt's first state `{ninth, mercury}`; and `flags` `{ratandha, nabalig, dharmi, sathi}`. `cycle` is the 35-year cycle's start `{planet, year}` and `periods` its periods `{planet, from, to}` over years 1 to 120 of life. `year` is `{year, ruler, thirds, annual}`, `annual` the annual teva's reading in the same shape when the record sent a `varshphal` list, otherwise null; `year` itself is null unless the record named one. Grahas are bare catalogue keys. Empty when `lalkitab_json` asked for none.
  final String lalkitab;

  /// What each chart's instant falls in, a row a chart in the `cast` section's order: the sign rising and its span, which BPHS ch. 92 v. 4's lagna gandanta reads, and the eclipse seen where the chart is cast, which Brihat Jataka ch. 6 v. 9 reads. Empty when the moment was not asked for.
  final ChartsMoment moment;

  /// Every stretch of life a progressed planet stands within the orb of a radical point's distance from the equator, on either side of it (Leo, *The Progressed Horoscope*, p. 34), concatenated in the `cast` section's order and **ragged** by `progressions.parallel_count`, each chart's in the order of its closest instant. Empty when `progressions_json` asked for none.
  final ChartsProgressedParallels progressedParallels;

  /// Every exact aspect two progressed planets make to each other in the record's window (Leo's "P. to P." list, *The Progressed Horoscope*, p. 41), each pair once in the order the record names the planets, concatenated in the `cast` section's order and **ragged** by `progressions.mutual_count`, each chart's in the order they fall due. Empty when `progressions_json` asked for none.
  final ChartsProgressedMutualContacts progressedMutualContacts;

  /// The Black Moon Lilith beside the nine, **one row a chart** when the request's `lilith` named an apogee and empty when it did not, in the columns `grahas` has but its first: the apogee rather than a graha. It is placed in the chart's zodiac and from its centre, as the nine are (C441). The mean apogee is a direction on the ecliptic, so its latitude and distance are zero; the osculating one carries the ellipse's own, and is the only one ever retrograde (C439, C440).
  final ChartsLilith lilith;

  /// The sthira karakas of BPHS ch. 32 vv. 18 to 20, ten a chart in the table's order, charts outermost: row `i * 10 + k` is the `i`th chart in `jaimini`, karaka `k`. The father's and the mother's are the stronger of their pair (C408, C409); `chosen_by` says how. Empty when the Jaimini reading was not asked for.
  final ChartsJaiminiSthiraKarakas jaiminiSthiraKarakas;

  /// The karaka bhavas of BPHS ch. 32 vv. 22 to 24, seven a chart in the table's order, charts outermost: row `i * 7 + k` is the `i`th chart in `jaimini`, row `k`. Each is the house counted from a graha's sign, whole signs in the rasi chart, and the sign it falls in. Empty when the Jaimini reading was not asked for.
  final ChartsJaiminiKarakaBhavas jaiminiKarakaBhavas;

  /// Each chart's dispositors under the traditional rulers, a row a chart in `dignities`, charts outermost. Empty when the dignities were not asked for.
  final ChartsDispositions dispositions;

  /// The seven's chains of dispositors, seven a chart in the order `dignity_planets` gives them, each followed until a planet repeats.
  final ChartsDispositorChains dispositorChains;

  /// Each chain's dispositors, ragged by `step_count`: its dispositor, that planet's, and so on, up to the last before the first that repeats; none for a planet in its own sign.
  final ChartsDispositorSteps dispositorSteps;

  /// Where each chart's chains stop, each once, ragged by `end_count`, in the order the chains first reach them.
  final ChartsDispositorEnds dispositorEnds;

  /// Each end's planets, ragged by `member_count`: the one in its own sign, or a cycle's from its slowest member, each in the next one's sign and the last in the first's.
  final ChartsDispositorEndMembers dispositorEndMembers;

  /// UTF-8 JSON, canonical: an array with one entry per chart, each an array with one reading per instant of the record, in its order (`03-design/gochar.md` §8). A reading is `{rules, native, grahas, points, maleficPoints}`. `rules` is `{front, sight, corner}`. `native` is `{nakshatra, rashi, tithi, vara, name}`, `name` `{letter, vowel}` and left out when the record named none. `grahas` is the nine, the Sun to Ketu, each `{graha, place, motion, lines, nature, waning, joinedBy, cells, points}`: `place` `{star, nakshatra, pada}` with `star` `{star: "NAKSHATRA", nakshatra}` or `{star: "ABHIJIT"}`; `motion` `FAST`, `MEAN` or `RETROGRADE`; `lines` among `LEFT`, `FRONT` and `RIGHT`; `nature` `BENEFIC` or `MALEFIC`; `cells` each reach `{by: "LINE", line, cell}`, `{by: "CORNER", cell}` or `{by: "STANDS"}`, a cell tagged by `cell` as `STAR` (`star`), `VOWEL` (`vowel`), `LETTER` (`letter`, one Devanagari character), `RASHI` (`rashi`) or `TITHI` (`class`); and `points` each `{point, by}`. `points` is each of the native's points `{point, malefics, benefics}`, `point` among `NAKSHATRA`, `LETTER`, `VOWEL`, `TITHI`, `RASHI` and `VARA`. `maleficPoints` counts v. 28's five a malefic strikes. Catalogue members are bare keys. Empty when `sarvatobhadra_json` asked for none.
  final String sarvatobhadra;

  /// UTF-8 JSON, canonical: an array with one entry per chart, each an array with one row per year found, `1` up, in order (`03-design/tithi-pravesha.md`). A row is `{year, at, solarReturn, elongationDeg, rule, picked, inSign}`: `year` counted as `praveshas.year` counts it; `at` the instant the Moon's elongation from the Sun returns to the birth's, a UTC Julian day, where the year's chart is founded; `solarReturn` the year's sidereal solar return, UTC; `elongationDeg` the birth's directed elongation, `[0, 360)`; `rule` the rule asked for and `picked` the rule that chose the instant, `NATAL_SIGN` or `NEAREST_RETURN`, which differ where the natal sign held no phase return (C446); `inSign` how many phase returns fell while the Sun was in its natal sign, 0 to 2. A chart can hold fewer rows than `through` asked for where the ephemeris ends first. Empty when `tithi_pravesha_json` asked for none.
  final String tithiPravesha;

  /// UTF-8 JSON, canonical: an array with one string per chart, its dossier for a language model (`03-design/dossier.md`): the line `# teistro dossier N`, `N` the format's version, a legend of the sections written, then each section as a `== NAME ==` banner, a `#` header naming its `|`-separated columns, and its rows. The same chart under the same record is the same text. Empty when `dossier_json` asked for none.
  final String dossier;

  /// UTF-8 JSON, canonical: an array with one entry per chart, each an array of rows in order (`03-design/annual-chart.md`, "The month's and the day's chart"). A row is `{year, month, day, at, sunDeg}`: `year` counted as `praveshas.year` counts it; `month` 1 to 12; `day` 1 to 30; `at` the instant, a UTC Julian day, where the chart is founded; `sunDeg` where the Sun stands then in the year's zodiac, the annual Sun a sign further each month and the month's Sun a degree further each day (*Tajika Nilakanthi*, Saṃjñā Tantra, the monthly and daily entry, v. 1). Without `month` the rows are the year's twelve months, each as its first day, `day` 1; with it, that month's thirty days. Where the record names a `place`, each month's row carries `masesha`, its lord (`03-design/varshesha.md`, "The month's lord"): `{graha, reading, bearers, chain}`, `graha` the lord, a bare catalogue key; `reading` `CHAIN` or `LAGNA_LORD`; `bearers` the six office-bearers `{masaLagna, muntha, janmaLagna, triRashi, dinaRatri, varshaLagna, byDay}`; `chain` the year lord's chain read over them, `{graha, chosen, vishwa, claims, moonPassedOver}` as the year's lord is, `vishwa` and each claim's in sub-sub-units (3600 to a unit) and each claim `{graha, vishwa, aspectsLagna, portfolios}`. Beside it each such row carries `results`, the month's results ("The month's results"): `{houses, lords}`, `houses` the twelve `{house, amshaLord, lordAmshaLord, clauses, seenByAmshaLord, seenByMoon}`, `house` 1 to 12 by whole signs from the month lagna, `amshaLord` the lord of the navamsha the house's point falls in and `lordAmshaLord` that of the navamsha its sign lord stands in, bare catalogue keys; `clauses` those of vv. 7–11 that hold, each `FRIENDLY`, `MOON_FRIENDLY`, `INIMICAL`, `MOON_INIMICAL`, `LOW_AND_SET`, `BOTH_LOW`, `BOTH_SET`, `ONE_PLANET`, `STRONG` or `WEAK`; `seenByAmshaLord` and `seenByMoon` the lords of v. 10 each sees, each `VARSHA_LAGNA`, `MASESHA`, `VARSHESHA` or `MASA_LAGNA`; `lords` the five `{office, graha, house, clauses}`, `office` one of those four or `MUNTHA`, `clauses` those of vv. 12–13 that hold, each `TRIKA`, `WITH_MALEFIC`, `MALEFIC_INIMICAL`, `STRONG` or `WELL_PLACED`. Each such row carries `dasha` too, the month's dasha ("The month's dasha"): `{office, graha, sign, rules, periods}`, `office` `MUNTHA` or `MASA_LAGNA`, whose lord was the stronger; `graha` that lord and `sign` the sign whose Huddas run the month, bare catalogue keys; `rules` `{sign, clock, table}` as the record asked; `periods` the sign's five Huddas in order, each `{lord, degrees, starts, ends}`, `degrees` the Hudda's width and `starts` and `ends` UTC Julian days. Where the record names a `month` and a `place`, each day's row carries `dinesha`, its lord ("The day's lord"): `{graha, reading, bearers, chain}` as `masesha` is, `bearers` the seven `{muntha, janmaLagna, triRashi, dinaRatri, dinaLagna, masaLagna, varshaLagna, byDay}`; and `dayResults`, the day's results ("The day's results"): `{moonState, houses, lords, clauses}`, `moonState` the Moon's state within her sign, each `PRAVASA`, `NASHTA`, `MRITA`, `JAYA`, `HASYA`, `RATI`, `KRIDITA`, `PRASUPTA`, `BHUKTA`, `JVARA`, `KAMPITA` or `SUSTHITA`; `houses` the twelve `{house, amshaLord, clauses}`, `clauses` those of vv. 20–21 that hold, each `WITH_BENEFIC`, `BENEFIC_FRIENDLY`, `MOON_FRIENDLY`, `WITH_MALEFIC` or `MALEFIC_INIMICAL`; `lords` the four `{office, graha, house, clauses}`, `office` `DINESHA`, `VARSHESHA`, `MASESHA` or `MUNTHA` and `clauses` as the month's lords'; `clauses` those about the whole chart that hold, each `BENEFICS_WELL_PLACED_FROM_LAGNA`, `BENEFICS_WELL_PLACED_FROM_MOON`, `MALEFICS_WELL_PLACED_FROM_LAGNA`, `MALEFICS_WELL_PLACED_FROM_MOON`, `MALEFICS_FLANK`, `BENEFIC_TWELFTH`, `PAPA_KARTARI`, `SHUBHA_KARTARI`, `WANING_MOON_AFFLICTED`, `MOON_MARS_DUSTHANA`, `MALEFIC_FOURTH`, `BENEFIC_SEVENTH`, `BENEFIC_SECOND` or `BENEFIC_NINTH`. A chart holds no rows where the ephemeris ends before the year does. Empty when `masa_pravesha_json` asked for none.
  final String masaPravesha;

  /// UTF-8 JSON, canonical: an array with one entry per chart, each an array of the shapes its planets make, by kind in the order `GRAND_TRINE`, `T_SQUARE`, `GRAND_CROSS`, `YOD`, `KITE`, `MYSTIC_RECTANGLE`, `STELLIUM`, and within a kind by the bodies' order (`03-design/western-configurations.md`). A shape is `{kind, bodies, apex, sign, widestFromExactDeg, inside}`: `kind` one of those keys; `bodies` the grahas, bare catalogue keys (`SUN`); `apex` the graha a T-square, yod or kite points at, null for the others; `sign` the tropical rashi a stellium stands in, bare (`LEO`), null for the others; `widestFromExactDeg` how far from exact its loosest aspect is, degrees, null for a stellium; `inside` the positions in the chart's array of the larger shapes this one is wholly inside, empty when it stands alone. Every shape is made of aspects the chart holds under the record's `aspects` and `orbs`. Empty when `western_configurations_json` asked for none.
  final String westernConfigurations;

}

/// Decodes a Charts blob. The columns are views over `bytes`, so the
/// buffer must outlive the result; a blob of another layout version or
/// another schema is a [FormatException].
Charts decodeCharts(Uint8List bytes) {
  final blob = _Blob.open(bytes, 3, 'charts');
  final atSummary = blob.fixed(1, 'summary', 8);
  final atCast = blob.section(2, 'cast');
  final atGrahas = blob.section(3, 'grahas');
  final atReadings = blob.fixed(4, 'readings', 6);
  final atHouses = blob.section(5, 'houses');
  final atChalit = blob.section(6, 'chalit');
  final atZodiac = blob.fixed(7, 'zodiac', 3);
  final atDay = blob.section(8, 'day');
  final atTiming = blob.section(9, 'timing');
  final atModel = blob.section(10, 'model');
